---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';

---

<Layout
  title="Stand Out Trello Guide & Game Directory | Stand Out Wiki"
  description="Comprehensive breakdown of the Roblox STAND OUT Trello directory. Learn how movesets, 55 documented Stands (51 playable), drop percentages, gardening, and patch notes are organized."
  canonicalPath="trello"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Trello Guide' }]}
  schemaType="Article"
  dateModified="2026-11-26"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 md:py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-10 pb-8 border-b border-slate-200">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider mb-3 border border-emerald-200">
        <span>Game Architecture &amp; Data Roadmap</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Stand Out Trello Guide &amp; Database Directory
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        Many players look for the developer Trello to check raw card notes, move cooldowns, and agricultural formulas for Studio Umbra's <strong>STAND OUT</strong>. This guide explains how the board is structured and directs you to our verified, searchable Wiki pages.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick Navigation Hub -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 mb-12">
      <a href="/stands/" class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 hover:border-emerald-500 hover:shadow-xs transition-all block text-center">
        <span class="text-xs font-black text-slate-900 block">55 Stands Database</span>
        <span class="text-[11px] text-emerald-700 font-semibold mt-1 block">Browse Movesets →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/codes/" class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 hover:border-emerald-500 hover:shadow-xs transition-all block text-center">
        <span class="text-xs font-black text-slate-900 block">Active Codes</span>
        <span class="text-[11px] text-emerald-700 font-semibold mt-1 block">View Codes →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/stand-arrows/" class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 hover:border-emerald-500 hover:shadow-xs transition-all block text-center">
        <span class="text-xs font-black text-slate-900 block">Arrow Drop Rates</span>
        <span class="text-[11px] text-emerald-700 font-semibold mt-1 block">Check Math →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/updates/" class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 hover:border-emerald-500 hover:shadow-xs transition-all block text-center">
        <span class="text-xs font-black text-slate-900 block">Update Timeline</span>
        <span class="text-[11px] text-emerald-700 font-semibold mt-1 block">Read Patches →</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Sections -->
    <div class="space-y-10 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Section 1 -->
      <section class="bg-white p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">1. What Is the Stand Out Trello?</h2>
        <p>
          The developer Trello board is an internal planning and documentation tool maintained by <strong>Studio Umbra: Europa</strong>. It serves as an unstyled, raw card index where developers post animation preview GIFs, move cooldowns, patch changelogs, and work-in-progress character balance notes.
        </p>
        <p>
          While the board contains over 800 cards across 34 categories, raw cards are often fragmented, split across multiple attachments (such as King Crimson being split into separate Doppio and Boss cards), or contain temporary developer shorthand. Our Wiki compiles this raw information into structured, interactive pages with calculators, search filters, and side-by-side comparisons.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2 -->
      <section class="bg-white p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">2. Stand Categories &amp; Rarity Structure</h2>
        <p>
          On the official board, characters are cataloged across three primary lists:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
            <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 text-xs mb-1 uppercase tracking-wider">Stands (Arrow)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
              41 live playable Stands awakened via Mysterious, Lucky, or Bizarre Arrows across Rare, Epic, Legendary, Mythical, and Pinnacle tiers (including Kiss and Part 9 stands).
            </p>
            <a href="/stands/" class="text-[11px] font-bold text-emerald-700 mt-2 block">View Arrow Stands →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
            <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 text-xs mb-1 uppercase tracking-wider">Evolution &amp; Exclusive</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
              Specialized evolutions and leaderboard exclusives including SPTW, TWAU, Jojosapiens, and Heaven's Door Prime.
            </p>
            <a href="/guides/evolve-stands/" class="text-[11px] font-bold text-emerald-700 mt-2 block">Evolution Guide →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
            <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 text-xs mb-1 uppercase tracking-wider">In Testing / Previews</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
              Upcoming prototypes currently listed on developer testing boards (Made in Heaven, Rock Human Part 8 placeholder); Crazy Diamond and The Lock have now graduated to live release.
            </p>
            <a href="/updates/" class="text-[11px] font-bold text-emerald-700 mt-2 block">Patch Timeline →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3 -->
      <section class="bg-white p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">3. How to Find Stand Movesets &amp; Frame Data</h2>
        <p>
          On Trello, movesets are broken down into individual subheadings with animation webps and base cooldown lines. To view complete, cleanly formatted movesets without hunting through scattered attachments, use our dedicated Stand pages:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-xs">
          <li><strong>Pinnacle Tier:</strong> Full combo guides for <a href="/stands/star-platinum/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">Star Platinum</a>, <a href="/stands/the-world/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">The World</a>, and <a href="/stands/king-crimson/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">King Crimson</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Defensive Tanks:</strong> Mechanics breakdown for <a href="/stands/yellow-temperance/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">Yellow Temperance</a> and <a href="/stands/notorious-big/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">Notorious B.I.G</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Disruption &amp; Tactical:</strong> Kinetic manipulation for <a href="/stands/kraft-work/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">Kraft Work</a> and fate timers for <a href="/stands/rolling-stones/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">Rolling Stones</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4 -->
      <section class="bg-white p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">4. Arrow Rates &amp; Obtainment Information</h2>
        <p>
          The developer board confirms official drop rates for all summon items:
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <table class="w-full text-xs text-left">
            <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[11px]">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-3">Arrow Type</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3">Pinnacle Rate</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3">Excluded Tiers</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3">Obtainment Method</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 font-mono">
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-bold text-slate-900">Mysterious Arrow</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-slate-600">0.50%</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-slate-600">None (Full Pool)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-slate-600">Story Quests, Bounties, Map Spawns</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-bold text-slate-900">Lucky Arrow</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-emerald-700 font-bold">1.50%</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-slate-600">Rare Filtered</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-slate-600">Crafting Bench (3 Scrap + 1 Arrow)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-bold text-slate-900">Bizarre Arrow</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-purple-700 font-bold">4.40%</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-slate-600">Rare &amp; Epic Filtered</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-slate-600">Passione Train Raid Boss Drops</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">
          Use our interactive <a href="/stand-arrows/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">Arrow Calculator</a> to simulate pull probabilities and pity thresholds.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5 -->
      <section class="bg-white p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">5. Game Mechanics &amp; Systems</h2>
        <p>
          STAND OUT features complex secondary systems documented across various Trello categories:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
          <a href="/gardening/" class="p-3 bg-slate-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 block transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 block">Gardening &amp; Greenhouses</span>
            <span class="text-slate-500 text-[11px] mt-0.5 block">Crop growth times, 3x gang buffs, and produce export stalls.</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/rokakaka/" class="p-3 bg-slate-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 block transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 block">33 Rokakaka Mutations</span>
            <span class="text-slate-500 text-[11px] mt-0.5 block">3% base mutation rates, stone limb penalties, and equivalent exchange.</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/hamon/" class="p-3 bg-slate-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 block transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 block">Hamon Sub-Ability</span>
            <span class="text-slate-500 text-[11px] mt-0.5 block">Jonathan, Caesar, and Zeppeli Ripple breathing specializations.</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/vampire/" class="p-3 bg-slate-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 block transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 block">Vampirism &amp; Stone Mask</span>
            <span class="text-slate-500 text-[11px] mt-0.5 block">Blood meter siphon, Space Ripper Stingy Eyes, and Shadow Cloaks.</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: FAQ -->
      <section class="bg-white p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">6. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-xs mb-1">Where do I find newly announced codes on Trello?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
              Codes are announced in developer changelog cards and patch announcements, rather than a single static card. We track all active and expired promo codes on our <a href="/codes/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">Codes Page</a> with verification notes.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-xs mb-1">What is the actual maximum level cap in STAND OUT?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
              According to the updated official Stats card, the live maximum level is <strong>Level 75</strong>. Each level awards 3 Stat Points, granting <strong>225 total Stat Points</strong> to allocate across Health, Damage, and Ability (with a verified 166 single-stat cap per the Nov 16 combat update). An older legacy card listed Level 50 / 150 SP.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-xs mb-1">How often does Studio Umbra release game updates?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
              Patches, raid tuning, and bug fix updates typically roll out weekly. You can track full version changelogs on our <a href="/updates/" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">Updates Timeline</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
